From: Erik Schnetter <schnetter@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: check for xlocale.h

Since 2.18.0, src/fcint.h and src/fcstr.c include <xlocale.h> if
HAVE_XLOCALE_H is defined, and fcint.h unconditionally uses locale_t
and the LC_*_MASK constants.  The Meson build checks for xlocale.h,
but configure.ac was never updated, so HAVE_XLOCALE_H is never defined
by the Autotools build.  On platforms where those declarations live in
<xlocale.h> rather than <locale.h> (macOS, FreeBSD) the build then
fails with "unknown type name 'locale_t'" and "use of undeclared
identifier 'LC_CTYPE_MASK'".

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@
 AC_CHECK_INCLUDES_DEFAULT
 AC_PROG_EGREP
 
-AC_CHECK_HEADERS([dirent.h fcntl.h stdlib.h string.h unistd.h sys/statvfs.h sys/vfs.h sys/statfs.h sys/param.h sys/mount.h])
+AC_CHECK_HEADERS([dirent.h fcntl.h stdlib.h string.h unistd.h sys/statvfs.h sys/vfs.h sys/statfs.h sys/param.h sys/mount.h xlocale.h])
 AX_CREATE_STDINT_H([src/fcstdint.h])
 
 # Checks for typedefs, structures, and compiler characteristics.
